  "content": {
    "id": "p13-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "Find positive integers $(x,y)$ for which $x-y,\\ 6,\\ x+y$ are in geometric progression.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p13-q14-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "(x,y)=(10,8)",
                "display": false
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p13-q14-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Use ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "(x-y)(x+y)=36",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " and consider factor pairs of the same parity.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "The square of the middle term equals the product of the outer terms:\n$$\\begin{align*}6^2&=(x-y)(x+y)\\\\36&=x^2-y^2.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $x,y>0$, both factors are positive and $x-y<x+y$. They have the same parity. Both cannot be odd because their product is even, so both are even. The even factor pairs of $36$ are $(2,18)$ and $(6,6)$. The pair $(6,6)$ gives $y=0$, so it is excluded.\n$$\\begin{align*}x-y&=2\\\\x+y&=18\\\\2x&=20\\\\x&=10\\\\y&=8.\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: the terms are $2,6,18$, with common ratio $3$. Thus $(x,y)=(10,8)$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 55
  },
